Run master.py to gather and prepare the data (Datastream sample -> TRTH 5-minute metrics -> merged panels).
All outputs are Parquet; the analysis stage (../analysis) reads data/03_output/*.parquet.

Step by step:
  python src/d00_gathering/sample.py                  -> data/02_preprocessed/sample.csv (Datastream, USD)
  python src/d01_preprocessing/trth.py [options]      -> data/02_preprocessed/trth/ukraine*.parquet
  python src/d00_gathering/fx_rates.py   -> data/01_raw/handcoded/{fx_rates_ecb,venue_currency}.csv (ECB reference rates,
                                            currency and unit factor of each venue; run once before merge.py)
  python src/d02_panels/merge.py   (dollar volume and depth value converted to USD with the ECB rate of the venue's currency;
                                   excluded listings and implied-rate venues in analysis/output/tables/fx_diagnostics.csv)                      -> data/03_output/{intraday,daily,...}.parquet

TRTH preprocessing (two phases: stage shards per ric x LOCAL trading day, then compute 5-minute metrics):
  python src/d01_preprocessing/trth.py --phase2-workers 8 --output-format parquet --timings
  Phase 1 shards in data/02_preprocessed/tmp are reused when present (a completed staging carries a
  _PHASE1_COMPLETE marker); delete a staging folder to re-stage from the raw .csv.gz.
  --engine polars --temp-format parquet  : polars engine (parity-tested against pandas)
  --direction tick|fi|both               : trade direction (default both): Lee-Ready (quote rule + tick rule) and the
                                           Jurkatis (2022, JFM) full-information algorithm (vendored in
                                           src/d01_preprocessing/tradeclass/, MIT; build once with
                                           `python setup.py build_ext --inplace` inside that folder)
  --winsor-ticks                         : tick-level winsorization per ric at 0.01%/99.99% (default OFF)
  src/d01_preprocessing/validate_fi.py   : FI vs tick-test validation on random real shards
  src/d01_preprocessing/count_tick_filters.py : exact counts of crossed/stub quotes and bad prints per file
  --auto-tune                            : chunk size / workers from RAM and CPU
  --generate-sample                      : small synthetic .csv.gz for testing

Cleaning applied at the tick level: ask < bid quotes, negative prices/volumes, stub quotes
((ask-bid)/mid > 25%) and trades more than 50% away from the prevailing midpoint are dropped.

Tested on Sep 3, 2026 - MacBook Pro M4 Max, 32GB, macOS 26.1.
